== The Standing-Wave Hazard ==

When <math>Z_{\rm device} \neq Z_{\rm bio}</math>, the forward-propagating and reflected ψ waves superpose to produce a standing wave pattern in the space between device and operator:

:<math>|\psi(x)|^2 = |A|^2\,\bigl|e^{ikx} + \Gamma\,e^{-ikx}\bigr|^2 = |A|^2\bigl(1 + |\Gamma|^2 + 2|\Gamma|\cos(2kx + \phi)\bigr)</math>

The standing wave has spatial maxima (antinodes) at positions:

:<math>x_n = \frac{n\pi - \phi/2}{k}, \quad n = 0, 1, 2, \ldots</math>

At an antinode, the ψ field amplitude is <math>|A|(1 + |\Gamma|)</math> — enhanced above the forward-wave amplitude by a factor <math>(1 + |\Gamma|)</math>. At a node, it is <math>|A|(1 - |\Gamma|)</math> — reduced.

=== ψ-Dependent Hazard Assessment (Track B) ===

If ψ-charged biological tissue (the operator's cortex) is located at a standing-wave antinode, it experiences field intensity <math>(1 + |\Gamma|)^2</math> times the intended exposure — potentially well above the design operating point. For <math>|\Gamma| = 0.6</math> (moderate mismatch), the antinode intensity is <math>(1.6)^2 = 2.56</math> times nominal. The biological effect of such over-intensity is uncharacterised and represents the primary safety concern in misconfigured [[Psi-Tech]] devices.

The antinode spacing is <math>\lambda_\psi/2 = \pi/k</math>. At 40 kHz in the [[Psi Stabilizer]] design (k ≈ 5 m⁻¹ from [[ψ Boundary Conditions]]):

:<math>\text{antinode spacing} = \pi/k \approx \pi/5 \approx 0.63\,\text{m}</math>

At this wavelength, the standing-wave pattern is spatially coarse relative to head dimensions — a single antinode could span the full skull. This justifies the [[Anchor Controller]] safety interlock: any mismatch condition <math>|\Gamma|^2 > 0.4</math> must trigger amplitude reduction before the standing-wave pattern can establish.

