== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== Network Analysis and the ψ Smith Chart ===

RF engineers use the Smith chart — a conformal mapping of the complex impedance plane — to visualise and design matching networks. A ψ Smith chart would use the same mathematics, mapping complex <math>Z_\psi/Z_0</math> ratios in the unit disk. The key difference: because <math>Z_\psi</math> is frequency-dependent, the Smith chart trajectories under frequency tuning are not simple arcs but curves determined by <math>dZ_\psi/d\omega = -2/\omega^3 n_\psi</math>. This makes frequency-tuning a more complex matching strategy than in RF — but the HRV servo loop linearises the problem around the operating point.

=== Multi-Operator Impedance Networks ===

In a [[PsiNet]] node cluster, multiple operators with different <math>Z_{\rm bio}</math> values are simultaneously coupled to a shared ψ field. The network impedance seen by the field is the parallel combination:

:<math>Z_{\rm net} = \left(\sum_i \frac{1}{Z_{\rm bio}^{(i)}}\right)^{-1}</math>

The [[ψ Network Topology]] page (G3) derives the optimal coupling strategy for maximising total power transfer in a multi-operator network.

