{| class="wikitable" style="width:100%;"
! Limit !! Expected Result !! Verified?
|-
| <math>Z_1 = Z_2</math> || <math>\Gamma = 0</math>, <math>\tau = 1</math> — perfect match, no reflection || ✓
|-
| <math>Z_2 \to \infty</math> (open circuit) || <math>\Gamma \to 1</math>, <math>\tau \to 0</math> — total reflection, antinode at boundary || ✓
|-
| <math>Z_2 \to 0</math> (short circuit) || <math>\Gamma \to -1</math>, <math>\tau \to 0</math> — total reflection, node at boundary || ✓
|-
| <math>\omega \to \omega_c</math> (cutoff) || <math>n_\psi \to 0</math>, <math>Z_\psi \to \infty</math> — infinite impedance, no power propagates || ✓
|-
| <math>m_{\rm eff} \to 0</math>, high frequency || <math>Z_\psi \to 1/\omega^2</math> — frequency-dependent vacuum impedance; structurally consistent with massless scalar || ✓
|-
| <math>\tau</math> symmetric in <math>Z_1, Z_2</math> || <math>4Z_1Z_2/(Z_1+Z_2)^2 = 4Z_2Z_1/(Z_2+Z_1)^2</math> — transmission independent of which side the wave comes from || ✓
|}

